{{!< default}}
{{!-- Pages are standalone: no author box, no next/previous, no tags. A page
     that wants a post's furniture is a post. --}}
{{#post}}
<div class="ns-page ns-page--prose">
    {{!-- @page.show_title_and_feature_image is a per-page toggle in Ghost's
         editor, for a page that opens with its own designed hero and must
         not get a second title above it. gscan fails a page template that
         ignores it, and rightly: the switch is in the UI either way, so
         ignoring it makes the editor lie. --}}
    {{#if @page.show_title_and_feature_image}}
        <header class="ns-posthead">
            <div class="ns-posthead__inner">
                <h1 class="ns-posthead__title">{{title}}</h1>
                {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p class="ns-posthead__standfirst">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}
                {{#if feature_image}}
                    <img class="ns-posthead__cover" src="{{img_url feature_image size="xl"}}"
                         srcset="{{img_url feature_image size="l"}} 1000w, {{img_url feature_image size="xl"}} 2000w"
                         sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 1200px, 100vw"
                         alt="{{#if feature_image_alt}}{{feature_image_alt}}{{/if}}">
                {{/if}}
            </div>
        </header>
    {{/if}}

{{!-- gh-content AND ns-prose, and both are load-bearing.

         .ns-prose is NSDS's reading surface — 17px, 68ch, 1.7 leading.

         .gh-content is GHOST'S vocabulary, and without it 34 rules in
         assets/css/theme/ are dead. Ghost injects its own cards.min.css
         through {{ghost_head}} (card_assets: true) and that stylesheet was
         written against a white page: it hard-codes light-mode colours, a
         16px radius and a 1px border on every bookmark, callout and toggle
         card. theme/ghost.css restates each of those in NSDS's vocabulary —
         but every one of its selectors starts `.gh-content`, so with the
         class missing they never match and Ghost's own card CSS wins. That
         is the stray white bordered box inside an article on the navy
         surface. theme/reset.css also restores list markers under
         .gh-content, so bullets disappear without it too. --}}
    <div class="gh-content ns-prose">{{content}}</div>
</div>
{{/post}}
